2D Physics Engine

A custom 2D rigid-body physics engine built in C++ with a Python interface and Pygame visualization.

Features:
Collision Detection: SAT-based convex polygon collision detection with AABB broad-phase filtering.
Rigid-Body Dynamics: Simulates linear and angular motion, mass, and moment of inertia.
Collision Resolution: Sequential impulse solver with friction.
Constraints & Joints: Supports pivots, pendulum joints, and distance joints.
Compound Objects: Build complex objects from multiple primitive shapes.
Interactive Simulation: A game built on top of the engine that utilizies its features to showcase it..

Tech Stack:
C++
Python
Pygame
Pybind11

Overview:
Developed from scratch to explore rigid-body mechanics, collision detection, constraint solving, and numerical stability.

